                "The provided information confirms that global temperatures in 2025 were 1.3°C above pre-industrial levels[7], Arctic sea ice reached record-low extent in September[1][10], renewable energy provided 35% of global electricity[7], and carbon emissions from fossil fuels decreased 2% year-over-year while total atmospheric CO2 reached 425ppm[2][4].",
